{"cost_usd": 0.134466, "explanation": {"found": "missed  fix505 (domain)"}, "grade": {"chance": 0.0568, "findings": 2.0, "found": 0.0}, "in_tokens": 53778, "latency_s": 26.358, "meta": {"dropped_by_guardrails": 0, "findings_detail": [{"description": "The SRP_EPHEMERAL_WIDTH, SRP_SESSION_KEY_WIDTH, SRP_GENERATOR_WIDTH and SRP_RECONNECT_WIDTH constants are still defined in the AuthSocket.cpp anonymous namespace. This PR adds the same widths as Srp6::EphemeralWidth, SessionKeyWidth, GeneratorWidth and ReconnectWidth, and the challenge and reconnect-challenge packet builders still use the local copies. The proof maths and the packet serialisation can drift apart, which is the bug class this PR is trying to remove.", "file": "src/realmd/Auth/AuthSocket.cpp", "fix_sketch": "Delete the local SRP_* constants and use Srp6::EphemeralWidth, Srp6::SessionKeyWidth, Srp6::GeneratorWidth and Srp6::ReconnectWidth in the packet-building code.", "kind": "design", "line": 98, "severity": "low"}, {"description": "The 'short S' case sets shortS = true without asserting anything about S. The test file has no access to S, since only K is stored in the vector. The final CHECK(shortS && ...) therefore passes whenever a vector with that name exists, even if the search produced a vector where S is full width. The case is not actually pinned.", "file": "src/tests/Srp6Test.cpp", "fix_sketch": "Recompute S from the vector (A, v, u, b) in the test and CHECK S.GetNumBytes() < Srp6::EphemeralWidth, or store S in Srp6Vector.", "kind": "quality", "line": 115, "severity": "low"}], "per_bug": [{"bug": "fix505", "chance": 0.0568, "hits": [], "in_review": true, "located": false, "visible": "domain"}], "prompt_chars": 110490, "route_reasons": [], "routed_model": null, "tier": null, "unreviewed_files": ["src/tests/CryptoGoldenVectors.h"], "usage_calls": [{"completion_tokens": 2550, "completion_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 1982}, "cost": 0.129948, "cost_details